OL,3,GNEWSACommunity figures back ban on face
OL,4,Acoverings
OL,5,
OL,6,FSome West Midlands community figures
OL,7,Fhave welcomed a ban on face coverings
OL,8,Fin Nottingham city centre and say it
OL,9,Fshould also apply in their area.
OL,11,FFrom Tuesday, police and community
OL,12,Fprotection officers in the city can ask
OL,13,Fpeople to remove coverings if they
OL,14,F"reasonably believe" they are being
OL,15,Fused to conceal their identity to
OL,16,Fcommit crime or anti-social behaviour.
OL,18,FEnforcement will not apply to face
OL,19,Fcoverings worn for legitimate reasons,
OL,20,Fincluding religious, cultural, health,
OL,21,Fwork or personal safety.
OL,23,APub: 14-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
